    "w059": { "gloss": "evil", "note": "Latin “malo” can come from either the noun “malum,” evil, or “malus” used as a noun, the Evil One. The form alone does not distinguish these meanings. The grammatical description here corresponds to the first without excluding the petition’s personal reference.", "explanation": "The Catechism explains this petition as a prayer for deliverance from the Evil One, Satan (CCC 2851). It also includes deliverance from every evil (CCC 2854)." },
